+# Malware and Suspicious-Code Module
+
+## Enter When
+
+- a file, script, process, memory region, document, package, or network flow may implement malicious or covert behavior
+- the user needs behavior, configuration, IoCs, attribution limits, deobfuscation, protocol recovery, or detection content
+
+## Required Inputs
+
+- original sample/capture and SHA-256
+- acquisition source and expected platform
+- available isolation/reset environment
+- analysis question: behavior, config, family, protocol, extraction, or detection
+
+## Do
+
+1. Perform static triage before execution: type, architecture, signatures, metadata, imports, strings, resources, entropy, packer, embedded layers.
+2. Treat strings and automated detections as candidates; distinguish active paths, library artifacts, examples, and decoys.
+3. Select `scripts-and-obfuscation.md`, `pe-and-dotnet.md`, or `c2-and-protocols.md` from the bundled malware references.
+4. If dynamic execution is necessary, use an isolated resettable environment and capture process, file, registry, IPC, memory, and network effects.
+5. Extract configuration and protocol state with reproducible scripts; preserve each decoded layer.
+6. Build detections from proven behavior/config and note stable versus build-specific features.
+
+## Produce
+
+- identity/hash and static triage
+- observed behavior timeline
+- configuration/IoCs with provenance and confidence
+- extraction/decoder script
+- YARA/Sigma/network detection with tests when requested
+
+## Verification
+
+- reproduce config decoding from the original hash
+- corroborate active IoCs with execution, xrefs, config use, or decoded traffic
+- test detections on the target and at least one benign or neighboring sample
+- state unreached branches and anti-analysis limitations
+
+## Exit When
+
+The requested behavior/config/detection is reproducible, or a derived artifact is handed to Reverse, Forensics, or Crypto.
+
+## Read
+
+- `../../references/ctf/malware/index.md`
+- `../../references/malware.md`
+- exact topic path from `../../references/routing.md`
+
+### Deep references (malware analysis, merged)
+
+进入样本深度分析/检测规则编写阶段时按需取用（每次 1-2 篇）：
+
+- `references/malware-deep/yara-sigma-rules.md` — YARA/Sigma 规则编写与验证
+- `references/malware-deep/anti-analysis-techniques.md` — 反分析/反沙箱/反调试识别与绕过
+- `references/malware-deep/sandbox-orchestration.md` — 沙箱编排与动态行为采集
+- `references/malware-deep/_malware-workflow.md` — 完整恶意样本分析流程
